blocks.en:
In this chapter we give a brief discussion of the theory of linear operators $A$ from a Banach space $X$ to a Banach space $Y$. Our primary concerns center on the equation
\begin{equation}\label{eq:abstract-linear-operator-equation}
Ax=y,
\end{equation}
where $y\in Y$ is given, and the main issues we address are existence, multiplicity, and computability of solutions $x\in X$. Of course, most readers have already addressed these issues in studying linear algebra. There, the spaces $X$ and $Y$ are the finite-dimensional vector spaces $\mathbb{R}^n$ and $\mathbb{R}^m$, respectively, and $A$ is represented by an $m\times n$ matrix. We have already considered a more general type of operator in this text when we defined a bounded linear operator from one (possibly infinite-dimensional) Banach space to another in Definition~\ref{def:bounded-linear-mapping}. However, as we shall see below, many important operators in PDEs (and ODEs) are unbounded. The reader is strongly encouraged to compare the results of this section with the results of his or her old linear algebra text while keeping in mind the two main extensions of the theory: to spaces that are infinite-dimensional and to operators that are unbounded.

blocks.zh:
本章简要讨论从 Banach 空间 $X$ 到 Banach 空间 $Y$ 的线性算子 $A$ 的理论. 主要关注方程
\begin{equation}\label{eq:abstract-linear-operator-equation}
Ax=y,
\end{equation}
其中给定 $y\in Y$, 所讨论的主要问题是解 $x\in X$ 的存在性, 多重性和可计算性. 当然, 大多数读者在线性代数的学习中已经讨论过这些问题. 在那里, 空间 $X$ 和 $Y$ 分别为有限维向量空间 $\mathbb{R}^n$ 和 $\mathbb{R}^m$, $A$ 由一个 $m\times n$ 矩阵表示. 在本书的 Definition~\ref{def:bounded-linear-mapping} 中, 定义了从一个 (可能无穷维的) Banach 空间到另一个 Banach 空间的有界线性算子, 已经考察过一种更一般类型的算子. 然而, 正如下面将看到的, PDE (以及 ODE) 中许多重要算子无界. 强烈建议读者将本节结果与以前的线性代数教材中的结果比较, 同时记住理论的两项主要推广: 推广到无穷维空间, 以及推广到无界算子.

blocks.en:
The range of $(\mathcal{D}(A),A)$ is a subspace $\mathcal{R}(A)\subset Y$ defined by
\begin{equation}\label{eq:linear-operator-range-definition}
\mathcal{R}(A):=\{u\in Y\mid u=A(x),\quad\text{for some }x\in\mathcal{D}(A)\}.
\end{equation}
The null space of $(\mathcal{D}(A),A)$ is the subspace $\mathcal{N}(A)\subset X$ defined by
\begin{equation}\label{eq:linear-operator-null-space-definition}
\mathcal{N}(A):=\{x\in X\mid A(x)=0\}.
\end{equation}

blocks.zh:
$(\mathcal{D}(A),A)$ 的值域是由下式定义的子空间 $\mathcal{R}(A)\subset Y$:
\begin{equation}\label{eq:linear-operator-range-definition}
\mathcal{R}(A):=\{u\in Y\mid u=A(x),\quad\text{for some }x\in\mathcal{D}(A)\}.
\end{equation}
$(\mathcal{D}(A),A)$ 的零空间是由下式定义的子空间 $\mathcal{N}(A)\subset X$:
\begin{equation}\label{eq:linear-operator-null-space-definition}
\mathcal{N}(A):=\{x\in X\mid A(x)=0\}.
\end{equation}
